# LLM Engineering Course

## Repository layout

- **Upstream (course author):** `https://github.com/ed-donner/llm_engineering`
- **Your fork (origin):** `https://github.com/slavapa/llm_engineering`
- **Local clone:** this workspace

## Git workflow

1. Keep `origin` pointing at your fork (`slavapa/llm_engineering`).
2. Add upstream once: `git remote add upstream https://github.com/ed-donner/llm_engineering.git`
3. Sync course updates: `git fetch upstream && git merge upstream/main` (resolve conflicts in course files only).
4. Push your work: `git push origin main`.
5. Optional PR to upstream: put **shareable** solutions in `weekN/community-contributions/slavapa/` only.

## Personal vs shareable work

- **`weekN/slavapa/`** — personal course exercises; commit to your fork only, **never** upstream PR.
- **`weekN/community-contributions/slavapa/`** — polished contributions you may submit upstream (e.g. Playwright scraper).

## Exercise sites

Use these sites for exercises unless the user specifies otherwise:

- https://kabbalahmedia.info/en/
- https://www.michaellaitman.com/
- https://kabuconnect.com/

## Where to put your work

- **Do not modify** core course notebooks (`weekN/day*.ipynb`) unless explicitly asked.
- Personal exercises → `weekN/slavapa/` (fork only).
- Shareable contributions → `weekN/community-contributions/slavapa/` (optional upstream PR).
- Keep notebook outputs cleared before commits.
- Never commit `.env`, API keys, or the `temp/` folder.

## Environment

- Python venv: `.venv` — select `.venv (Python 3.12.x)` as the Jupyter kernel.
- API keys live in `.env` (already gitignored).
- Free alternative: Ollama — see `guides/09_ai_apis_and_ollama.ipynb`.

## Agent behavior

- Help understand code before writing solutions.
- Match existing course patterns (OpenAI SDK, `scraper.py` helpers, markdown summaries).
- Prefer minimal, focused diffs in community-contributions.
